#NEXUS

[ motta2025a_fig5: Paravian reduced consensus, tree 1. The Eumaniraptora node is one continuous vertical (checked at 1.7x; the blue upper part and the black lower part share it), so it is a 14-way polytomy; the unenlagiid node is 7-way. The node abbreviations PA, EUM, DR and UNEN are printed on the tree and expanded in the caption (Paraves, Eumaniraptora, Dromaeosauridae, Unenlagiidae); they are kept as printed internal labels, unlike numeral or letter keys. 29 tips, 2 polytomies (14, 7 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261122). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

